<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3236" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ā^prūgnus</span></b>  (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ā^prūnus</span></b> ),
			a, um, adj.
		aper, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the wild boar</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aprugnum callum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Pers. 2, 5, 4</span></i>
			 Ritschl; cf. <i><span class="en">id. Poen. 3, 2, 2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aprunus adeps,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					28, 11, 47, § 167</span></i>
			 Jan: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lumbus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 8,
					51, 78, § 210</span></i>
			. —Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ā^prūgna</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ā^prūna</span></b> ),
				ae, f. (sc. caro), <i>the
				flesh of a wild boar</i>, <i><span class="en">Capitol. Max.
				Jun. 2</span></i>.—A secondary form, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ā^prūgĭnĕus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i><span class="en">Sol.
		32</span></i>.</div>
